    "show_share": true,
    "description": "How anaesthesiologists manage postpartum haemorrhage (PPH) is one of the major factors defining its outcome. This is a crucial moment when a happy family occasion becomes a life-or-death emergency. Knowing what to do and how to do it will make the difference, but if you have never experienced this situation before how do you learn? Now is not the time to practice: a mother's life depends on what you do in that moment, so you need to have gained some competence beforehand. This is a classic indication for practicing in the safety of clinical simulation.",
